Venetium 0023 - ffmpeg for Windows ARM32: the GN wiring for the win/arm-neon config (codecs on, D13).

BATCH-ARM-1 section 3G, his decision 8 (ARM-1-DECISIONS.md). The config itself is a generated input, not part of this patch:
third_party/ffmpeg/chromium/config/Chrome/win/arm-neon/ (10 files, venetium/deps/arm-inputs.tsv), made by FFmpeg's own configure through
venetium/deps/ffmpeg-win-arm.sh (Chromium's build_ffmpeg.py cannot run on this tree as-is). 2 files:
- third_party/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_generated.gni: the ARM C and .S sources were gated on use_linux_config only; the gates now also take
  is_win && current_cpu == "arm" (hand-widened, as generate_gn.py would for this config: FFmpeg's own make -n on the generated config
  lists exactly the same 285 sources - 270 C + 15 .S; generate_gn.py itself needs every platform's build dir and is not run).
- third_party/ffmpeg/BUILD.gn: HAVE_VFP_ARGS=1 for is_win && current_cpu == "arm". Windows ARM32 is hard-float (FFmpeg's configure
  detected it from __ARM_PCS_VFP; Chromium's config post-processing comments the define out and leaves it to the build, which sets it
  only for posix). Without it the float NEON/VFP assembly is built for the soft-float convention and corrupts float math SILENTLY
  (float_dsp_neon assembles either way) - the conscious check his decisions ask for; runtime proof is device-only (HE-AAC/SBR decode).
Checked (RUNTIME, real arm-rt21 graph after gn gen): ffmpeg_internal builds: 285 objects, all ARMNT, the 15 .S with their functions.
A later FFmpeg roll's generate_gn.py run would drop the win/arm stanzas: re-apply this patch after a roll.

diff --git a/third_party/ffmpeg/BUILD.gn b/third_party/ffmpeg/BUILD.gn
index bdf0208..b1f9a06 100644
--- a/third_party/ffmpeg/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/ffmpeg/BUILD.gn
@@ -328,6 +328,18 @@ target(link_target_type, "ffmpeg_internal") {
     }
   }
 
+  if (is_win && current_cpu == "arm") {
+    # Windows ARM32 is hard-float: float/double arguments are passed in VFP
+    # registers. The arm assembly (libavutil/arm/asm.S, sbrdsp_neon.S, ...)
+    # must be assembled for that convention, i.e. with HAVE_VFP_ARGS=1.
+    # config.h leaves HAVE_VFP_ARGS undefined on purpose (build_ffmpeg.py
+    # comments it out: "selection is done by the chrome build"), and the posix
+    # block above does not run on Windows. Left undefined, sbrdsp_neon.S does
+    # not assemble and float_dsp_neon.S silently assembles for the soft-float
+    # register convention (wrong float arguments at run time).
+    asmflags = [ "-DHAVE_VFP_ARGS=1" ]
+  }
+
   if (is_fuchsia || (is_posix && !is_mac)) {
     defines += [
       "_ISOC99_SOURCE",
